🐳 Running Kafka via Docker (Confluent)
docker run -d --name zookeeper \
  -p 2181:2181 \
  -e ZOOKEEPER_CLIENT_PORT=2181 \
  confluentinc/cp-zookeeper

docker run -d --name kafka \
  -p 9092:9092 \
  -e KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT=host.docker.internal:2181 \
  -e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092 \
  -e KAFKA_OFFSETS_TOPIC_REPLICATION_FACTOR=1 \
  confluentinc/cp-kafka
📌 Create Topic

Inside Kafka container:

docker exec -it kafka bash

Then:

kafka-topics --create \
  --topic KafkaLabTopic \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --partitions 1 \
  --replication-factor 1

List topics:

kafka-topics --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
🔧 Application Configuration
application.properties
spring.kafka.bootstrap-servers=localhost:9092

# Consumer
spring.kafka.consumer.group-id=my-group
spring.kafka.consumer.auto-offset-reset=earliest
spring.kafka.consumer.key-deserializer=org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer
spring.kafka.consumer.value-deserializer=org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer

# Producer
spring.kafka.producer.key-serializer=org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer
spring.kafka.producer.value-serializer=org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer
📤 Send Message (Producer)

Endpoint:

POST /api/send?message=HelloKafka

Example using curl:

curl -X POST "http://localhost:8080/api/send?message=HelloKafka"
📥 Consume Message

Consumer is implemented using:

@KafkaListener(topics = "KafkaLabTopic", groupId = "my-group")
public void consume(String message) {
    System.out.println("Received: " + message);
}

It is automatically triggered when a message is published.

No manual invocation required.

